Hello [~accountid:5faa45acf7b30b006e3b121d] 

As discussed on slack, we need to amend our [agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bdPGB1rTZ8GQTo0b_oP4ra2s2QxSIQ58/edit] with SGX Mobility to reflect our mos recent agreement. 
We intend to send this updated agreement to SGX to review and countersign at the earliest possible time.

See summary here below and let me know if you require any further clarification.

_Follow-up to further discussion within SGX management and conversation with AB and Osi, we have agreed to the following changes to the business agreement. Kindly send us a clean copy for signature on Monday._ 

+*Key:*+

*Black: Initial SGX feedback*

{color:#0747a6}Blue: Bolt team response{color}

{color:#bf2600}Red: Final agreement based on conversation with Osi.{color}



*Bolt Duties and Obligation: Requesting to add a section for Bolt Duties and Obligations include but not limited to 1) Non engagement with SGX competitors for electric tricycle during the 2-year period. 2) Bolt KPI to ensure SGX riders can achieve their KPI.*

 

{color:#0747a6}We can’t agree to part (1) for 2 reasons: {color}

# {color:#0747a6}This would prevent us from onboarding anyone with a 3-wheeler or electric 3 wheeler. Even if we don’t financially support them - which is anticompetitive{color}
# {color:#0747a6}SGX won't be able to fill the need for our category plans in Nigeria alone.{color}

{color:#0747a6}We are committed to the partnership but can't close off anyone else given our position in the market. Is there anything we can add to the agreement to give you more comfort? {color}

{color:#bf2600}SGX gets right of first refusal for Bolt partnerships that want to scale beyond 500 vehicles. Right of first refusal with SGX applies only to electric 3-wheelers deals where there is co-financing/co-investment from Bolt.{color}

{color:#bf2600}Right of first Refusal period is 20 days maximum for any deal with the following conditions.{color}

* {color:#bf2600}SGX has to show capabilities to scale WITHIN the period of refusal.{color}
* {color:#bf2600}Demonstrate financial capabilities within the right of refusal period{color}
* {color:#bf2600}Demonstrate operational capacity within the right of refusal period{color}
* {color:#bf2600}Right of first refusal is limited to Lagos only.{color}

*Section 3.5 & 3.6: SGX is requesting that the penalty and\or commission bonus be based on “Finished trips per week” KPI only since this links to revenue. Thus, Bolt should state the minimum trip request per week per driver to ensure SGX Rider can achieve the set finished trips per week.*

{color:#0747a6}We are committed to adding a guarantee of sorts post-pilot (of the 200). We need to understand what the impacts are of the first 200 vehicles and what the actual are before we can formalize the guarantee. We can update wording to reflect this and add an addendum, detailing the guarantee post-pilot. We believe we are de-risking the pilot to an extent given our 30% upfront payment of the first 200 vehicles, vs 20% on the remaining balance. {color}

{color:#bf2600}We are aligned on this . The penalty will only apply after the 200{color}

*Section 3.6: Bolt to add a table for commission bonus*

{color:#0747a6}We'll be specific as to what the bonus is here. Not sure if a table is needed.{color}

{color:#bf2600}We are ok with Bolt response above.{color}

*Section 5.2: Requesting this section to include payment of pilot phase be based on proforma invoice from manufacturer/supplier in order to pay for the units so the manufacturer can ship the CKD parts before Jan 31. This proposed change captures our understanding that Pilot Fees will be paid in advance to enable orders for the vehicles to be placed, while Scale-Up fees will be paid after vehicles arrive at the territory.*

 

{color:#0747a6}We're aligned with upfront payment for the pilot phase (for speed of execution), but we request not to pay the supplier - but would rather pay SGX - as we are entering into a contract with SGX, not the supplier. SGX can then pay the supplier. We're also happy for you to submit the attached irrevocable order AND the pro-forma invoice as supporting docs. Is this acceptable? {color}

{color:#bf2600}Yes, this is acceptable to SGX.{color}

 

*Section 1: Definition - Vehicle Deployment City: Requesting this definition be expanded to multiple cities for flexibility and growth. Also, SGX board wants the 1000 units across multiple cities.*

{color:#0747a6}We're aligned. Generally expansion will happen with Bolt's collaboration, to areas where our demand needs it the most.  {color}

{color:#bf2600}SGX is aligned with this.{color}

*Additional request to include in Bolt Duties and Obligations section: Bolt to promote and advertise an “Electric Tricycle” segment to the public to accelerate customer engagement via Bolt App.*

{color:#0747a6}Aligned for general promotion/advertising purposes. If there are any specific needs/expectations we'll need to get confirmation from our global marketing and brand team. {color}

{color:#bf2600}SGX is aligned with this{color}

