{quote}{color:#bf2600}Please note that yourDriver Rating as it appears in your Bolt app is calculated as an average rating based on your ratings from the previous 365 days. Each rating is from 1 to 5, {color}{color:#bf2600}*_as provided by the driver_*{color}{color:#bf2600} at the end of each trip.{color}{quote}

should it not be “as provided by the rider”? Because the driver rating consists of ratings given by passengers to driver.



{quote}{color:#bf2600}Please also note that if your request pertains to specific{color}{color:#bf2600} *_rider ratings_*{color}{color:#bf2600} that affect your average rating, then we will be unable to provide you with this data. Data protection law requires a data controller such as ourselves to protect the rights of third parties, and disclosure of the requested data would violate the rights and freedoms of the relevant {color}{color:#bf2600}*_driver(s) that provided the rating(s)._*{color}{quote}

Again, is the requestor not a driver? If he is a driver, then he wants to know his driver ratings, which are provided by passengers to the driver. Please then adjust the wording.

Information needed to substantiate facts: 
- Driver's details (name, address etc);
- Address of the additional stop;
- Address and time when the drive ended.

