{color:#FF5630}*[ REQUIREMENT UPDATE 3 ]*{color} 

According to the Finnish Holiday act employee is entitled to 2 holiday days per every working month if the employment has lasted less than a year and 2,5 holiday days per every working month if employment has lasted more than a year. The holiday days entitlement is noticed based on the employment length during the holiday credit year.If employment starts at 02/2024, then up to the end of holiday credit year (31.03.2024) employee will be entitled to 2 holiday days per month, 2+ 2 days, as you mentioned before. Employee will be entitled to 2 holiday days at new/ starting holiday credit year (01.04.2024) also until employment has lasted at least 1 year. In this case the holiday entitlement changes from 2 days to 2,5 days *retro-actively* since the beginning of the holiday credit year.

{color:#00B8D9}*[ EXAMPLE: ]*{color} 

_(Period April 2022 - March 2023)_ EE Tuukka Tammela: he joined Bolt in June 2022 

_(Period April 2023 - March 2024)_ He earns 2 days per month *until* June 2023 (until he reaches his 1 year of service in June) and from June 2023 until April 2024 he starts accruing 2,5 days per month. {color:#6554C0}*[ ACCRUAL TO BE BASED ON YOS ]*{color} 

_(April 2024 - March 2025)_ By April 2024 he worked more than 1 year and reached a new balance period which means that we should retroactively assign him 2,5 days from April 2023 till June 2023

